1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,681
Section two.

2
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:10,793
We look inside a dbt project: its building blocks, the one configuration file every project has, and the folder structure we follow.

3
00:00:11,073 --> 00:00:13,675
Then we teach the agent those rules with a skill.

4
00:00:14,776 --> 00:00:17,250
A dbt project is just a folder.

5
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:21,349
The only required file is dbt project dot yml.

6
00:00:21,629 --> 00:00:26,301
Models live in the models folder, with YAML files that describe and test them.

7
00:00:26,581 --> 00:00:31,274
Seeds, snapshots, tests, macros and analyses each have their own folder.

8
00:00:31,554 --> 00:00:33,666
A connection profile says where to build.

9
00:00:34,766 --> 00:00:39,140
The page About dbt projects, version one, is the map of this course.

10
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:43,452
Its resources table lists every building block a project can have.

11
00:00:43,732 --> 00:00:49,684
Its project configuration table lists the settings we put in dbt project dot yml.

12
00:00:50,784 --> 00:00:54,282
Here is every block from that page, with the section that builds it.

13
00:00:54,562 --> 00:01:00,280
Models, sources, seeds, tests, macros, analyses, snapshots, docs and exposures.

14
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:05,168
The dashed blocks, like metrics and the semantic layer, are beyond this crash course.

15
00:01:06,268 --> 00:01:07,484
The settings we use.

16
00:01:07,764 --> 00:01:08,894
The project name.

17
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:10,518
Our own version number.

18
00:01:10,798 --> 00:01:16,665
A required dbt version range, so the project only runs on dbt version one.

19
00:01:16,945 --> 00:01:18,268
The connection profile.

20
00:01:18,548 --> 00:01:21,278
And the folder paths, which we keep at their defaults.

21
00:01:21,558 --> 00:01:23,798
Variables come later, in section ten.

22
00:01:24,898 --> 00:01:26,541
We write this file by hand.

23
00:01:26,821 --> 00:01:30,085
The interesting part is at the bottom: settings per folder.

24
00:01:30,365 --> 00:01:33,010
Staging and intermediate models become views.

25
00:01:33,290 --> 00:01:34,677
Marts become tables.

26
00:01:34,957 --> 00:01:38,093
The plus sign means this is a setting, not a folder name.

27
00:01:38,373 --> 00:01:41,402
From now on, the folder decides how a model is built.

28
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:44,806
dbt Labs recommends three layers.

29
00:01:45,086 --> 00:01:49,673
Staging is shaped like the source: one model per table, renamed and typed.

30
00:01:49,953 --> 00:01:52,108
Intermediate holds business logic.

31
00:01:52,388 --> 00:01:56,036
Marts are shaped like the business, and they are what analysts query.

32
00:01:57,136 --> 00:02:02,490
The structure guide puts it simply: move data from source-conformed to business-conformed.

33
00:02:02,770 --> 00:02:07,613
And the goal is consistency, so nobody wastes time deciding names and folders.

34
00:02:07,893 --> 00:02:10,709
That is exactly what we want the agent to follow.

35
00:02:11,809 --> 00:02:13,622
How does the agent learn these rules?

36
00:02:13,902 --> 00:02:18,041
With a skill: a Markdown file of instructions with a short description.

37
00:02:18,321 --> 00:02:23,697
What we read in the docs, we write into the skill, and the agent loads it whenever a task matches.

38
00:02:24,797 --> 00:02:26,440
This is our skill, shortened.

39
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,170
The dbt version.

40
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:29,816
Naming for each layer.

41
00:02:30,096 --> 00:02:34,853
Column conventions, like timestamps ending in at, and booleans starting with is.

42
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:39,741
And the key rule: code values come from the dictionary file, never from memory.

43
00:02:40,841 --> 00:02:43,892
Skills are app-wide, so every project can use them.

44
00:02:44,172 --> 00:02:51,361
M C P servers give the agent extra knowledge, like the dbt, DuckDB and Rosetta documentation.

45
00:02:51,641 --> 00:02:56,292
You can add your own with one link, for example the dbt documentation site.

46
00:02:57,392 --> 00:03:06,266
In the demo, we test the setup with an Ask mode question: what is the difference between a source and a seed, using the dbt version one docs.

47
00:03:06,546 --> 00:03:09,640
The agent should look it up, and tell us which page it used.
